  "query_preview": "/TONIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 404 AM EDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nEarly tonight, most of the activity will be out of central Kentucky. \nWinds will begin to ease as they veer towards the north. Skies will \ntry to clear and this could lead to areas of fog from earlier \nmoisture as temperatures fall into the mid 60s to low 70s.   \n\nBehind the front, surface high pressure will bring CAA and cooler \ntemperatures with highs in the upper 70s to mid 80s through Friday \nbefore the high passes to the east and WAA returns, brining mid 80s \nto low 90s back for the weekend. Dry weather is expect through the \nend of the workweek with low-end rain chances returning around the \nweekend into early next week as little surface systems ride in on \nnorthwest flow.",
